    {
      "id": "claim_70fc6d190e18496bb31f844eb4cc6579",
      "statement": "The project convention for a bounded context is a non-instantiated DependencyContextType mixed into local Feature and ApplicationService bases via multiple inheritance, so every service in the context inherits the declared dependency names as typed attributes; the checked typing example re-annotates context on those local bases because a handler's self.context type comes from the handler class, not from the dependency map.",
      "evidence": [
        {
          "resource": "repo://README.md#L412-L470",
          "version": "repo-lines-v1:sha256:1f271023f084dd557c0e216924bb43eee5da96f245c446e69045b22940b30ffc:"
        },
        {
          "resource": "repo://tests/typing_and_linter/typing_cases/typed_context_case.py#L29-L52",
          "version": "repo-lines-v1:sha256:e03da8e339bf0627c2430ecd4f161e5a755706ab6856215b68c095efb16c92b9:"
        }
      ]
    },
    {
      "id": "claim_0adc136fb96e4969ad5d1e4f43137e2f",
      "statement": "The routing key of a registration is the input DTO class __name__, written at registration and read at execution, and a DTO name may live in only one layer: each layer's decoration-time check inspects only its own registry, so a cross-layer collision passes decoration and is detected when FrameworkBus is constructed, with the documented remedy being to rename the DTO or use another framework instance.",
      "evidence": [
        {
          "resource": "repo://sincpro_framework/bus.py#L150-L162",
          "version": "repo-lines-v1:sha256:ed1f435d2c77cc7b7c37cda33e0b7e0f4b5980ab47d30de61a196a671d63b392:"
        },
        {
