    {
      "id": "claim_70d72d0843a4427cbcb78d92a4a23e27",
      "statement": "Verifying a bootstrap has two different gates: the declared-dependency check needs no build because framework.deps never touches self.bus, while reading registrations through introspection requires a built instance (features/app_services/dtos raise ValueError otherwise) and skips registry keys that are absent from dto_registry, which is why handlers wired through the bus-level register_feature / register_app_service API remain invisible to introspection and to every wire host.",
      "evidence": [
        {
          "resource": "repo://sincpro_framework/introspection/inspector.py#L72-L75",
          "version": "repo-lines-v1:sha256:8c0ed042aaf7565c3e34c7d8fd299364fbe38ed5bc622b71555f213510f2854f:"
        },
        {
          "resource": "repo://sincpro_framework/introspection/inspector.py#L83-L86",
          "version": "repo-lines-v1:sha256:2e761dd065b579de2a13aa1135685a49fa7c84e33ec68b7ea57235fe1e9a08d5:"
        },
        {
          "resource": "repo://tests/test_introspection.py#L76-L80",
          "version": "repo-lines-v1:sha256:d43fde86666b9f9fdefd5ed15cf26f275d3cc33ecf5fc02854b1e61eb0f43a66:"
        }
      ]
    },
    {
      "id": "claim_5c7a4ef3b3ed46e7af445e21da6904d8",
      "statement": "Building a bounded context eagerly is an operational choice for a service that also serves HTTP: invoking is lazy (the first framework(dto) builds), but building any bus is what installs the process-level OTel provider the transport middleware needs, so the service builds its buses before serving the first request.",
